    ],
    "text": "Summary"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000012",
    "issues": [
      "hyphen_join_review"
    ],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0016-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0017-l0000"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0017-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0018-l0000"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0018-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0019-l0000"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0016-l0000",
      "p0001-n0017-l0000",
      "p0001-n0018-l0000",
      "p0001-n0019-l0000"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "We construct two models to facilitate the construction of the Tesla network from a macro perspective, a double-layer complex network to measure the network topology and a SI epi- demic model based on the evaluation index system(SI-EI)to identify the key factors in the building process."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000013",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0020-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0021-l0000"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0021-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0022-l0000"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0022-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0023-l0000"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0020-l0000",
      "p0001-n0021-l0000",
      "p0001-n0022-l0000",
      "p0001-n0023-l0000"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "The double-layer complex network can be used to determine the number, location and distribution of chargeing stations. People are divided into long-distance and short-distance travelers. The number of charging stations are determined mainly by Vehicle Density, Daily Mileage and Range Anxiety: (1) the outer layer is to study the demands of long-distance trav-"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000014",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "title",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0024-l0000"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "elers for supercharge stations,with introduced Weighted Betweenness to measure whether a"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000015",
    "issues": [
      "hyphen_join_review"
    ],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0025-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0026-l0000"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0026-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0027-l0000"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0027-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0028-l0000"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0028-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0029-l0000"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0025-l0000",
      "p0001-n0026-l0000",
      "p0001-n0027-l0000",
      "p0001-n0028-l0000",
      "p0001-n0029-l0000"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "city is a traffic hub, which is the reference to arrange the location; (2) the inner layer is to study the demands of the remaining three cases, and arrange location according to Vehicle Densi- ty. The distribution is based on the number of the above four cases. We introduce Reachable Level, Permeability and Long-distance travel demand rate into SI-EI model to measure daily infection rate \u03bb, and apply the traditional SI model to determine the keyfactors."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000016",
    "issues": [
      "hyphen_join_review"
    ],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0030-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0031-l0000"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0031-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0032-l0000"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0030-l0000",
      "p0001-n0031-l0000",
      "p0001-n0032-l0000"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "For problem 1, there are 8.08 million destination charging stations and 2.16 million super- charge stations in the final network architecture. It takes 108 years to reach fully automobile electrification for constructed networks while it takes 36 years to construct networks."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000017",
    "issues": [
      "hyphen_join_review"
    ],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
