      "p0001-n0038-l0000",
      "p0001-n0039-l0000"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "For problem 2, we choose Ireland. There are 78 thousand destination charging stations and 20.8 thousand supercharge stations in the final network architecture. The optimal invest- ment plan is to establish a 2: 1 ratio between the scale of the site and the present required scale, and to establish charging stations by mixing the ratio of the city to the rural area to 3: 2. The conclusion is mainly building destination charging stations when Permeability is less than 30%, and building supercharge stations in cities when Permeability is less than 50%but more than 30%, otherwise building supercharge stations in roads."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000018",
    "issues": [],
